      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "It looks like I was not clear enough in my request.\nWhat I really meant to ask is if git syncing of the various SDK packages as well as having the files from the SDK be stored in the packages folder of Unity instead of the Assets would be possible *without* using any other application like the VCC or cli version. \nSorry for not being clear in my original post.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-05-18T18:25:31.750Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The VPM packaging format (at least how I hear it) is superior to dropping unitypackages into unity. The VCC sadly does not have a mac or linux version, which at this moment will force those creators to continue using the older packaging format. Since the VPM is built using Unity's native package manager, it should be simple enough to allow users to install the SDK using the VPM while also not using the VCC. Also, many people might not feel the need to use another launcher on top of unity hub or don't require/want to take advantage of the new features of the VCC, or they might prefer to manage their own projects. I see this becoming more important in extremely non-standard setups like my own.",
